{"id":"4d8b27fd-fa8e-4db1-94fd-10dc4b6c0450","object":"chat.completion","created":1784801032,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    names = [seg['name'] for seg in segments]\\n    minimums = [seg['minimum'] for seg in segments]\\n    capacities = [seg['capacity'] for seg in segments]\\n    importances = [seg['importance'] for seg in segments]\\n    sum_min = sum(minimums)\\n    sum_max = sum(capacities)\\n    if budget < sum_min or budget > sum_max:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget out of range')\\n    allocations = list(minimums)\\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        best_score = -1.0\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if allocations[i] < capacities[i]:\\n                score = importances[i] / (allocations[i] + 1)\\n                if score > best_score or (score == best_score and i < best_idx):\\n                    best_score = score\\n                    best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            break\\n        allocations[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    return {\\n        'allocations': allocations,\\n        'names': names,\\n        'total': sum(allocations)\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that returns a JSON-serializable object. The problem is a budget allocation across segments with importance, minimum quotas, capacities. Use a greedy algorithm: start with each segment at its minimum. Then while remaining budget >0, allocate one token to the segment with highest importance / (current allocation + 1) (i.e., next position). Break ties by original order (segment index). Ensure budget is exactly used, not exceeding total capacity. Reject if budget < sum of minimums or budget > sum of capacities.\n\nReturn allocations (list of segment names wit