ust, I'll validate and if invalid, return an error dict. But the fixtures seem valid. I'll assume valid.\n\n3. Initialize allocations array with minimums. Remaining = budget - sum_min.\n\n4. For each step while remaining >0:\n   - compute for each segment: if current allocation < capacity, then score = importance / (allocation + 1). Else score = -inf (or skip).\n   - pick segment with max score; tie break by original order.\n   - increment allocation, decrement remaining.\n\n5. After loop, allocations equal budget.\n\n6. Return dict with \"allocations\" list, \"names\" list (in order), \"total\" (budget).\n\nBut careful: The names should be in the same order as segments. The output likely expects list of allocation amounts corresponding to the segment names.\n\nImplementation details: Use list of segments with indices.\n\nEdge case: segments may have name duplicates? Probably not.\n\nNow produce Python source code. Use def solve(case): ... return result.\n\nImportant: Use only standard library (no numpy, etc.).\n\nThe output must be a single JSON with key \"implementation\" and value being the Python source string escaped.\n\nLet's write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1038,"completion_tokens":1123,"total_tokens":2161,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1024},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":806},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1024,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":14},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}